ith its Ionic portico and broad steps to Elmwood Avenue, porches at its ends, a low metal roof with the galleries' skylight; Gordon Bunshaft's 1962 Knox building to the north, marble walls round the sculpture court (now roofed by Common Sky, the faceted glass canopy of 2023 on its one spreading column) and the black glass box of the auditorium; OMA's Gundlach Building (2023) at the north-west corner, a marble volume wrapped in curved glass; Hoyt Lake's edge and the park's trees to the south-east. From the museum's campus pages, Architectural Record, Buffalo Architecture and History, WNY History; guessed: the plan dimensions, the order of columns, the ends' porches (the real building has caryatid porches), the Gundlach's fluted glass as ribs, the link between the buildings. No photographs were available."}